 "notes": "Degradation paper: PRC/stimulus is the salt test; decay forms are PRP/behavior_class (degradation mode) and the solution ranking PRF/service_capability. Two spine branches from the test: physical (salt location -> crystallization pressure -> fissures -> decay forms) and chemical (reaction products -> cement dissolution -> bimodal porosity). Tension: F4 shows intense fissuring after diluted solutions, while the paper argues large-pore precipitation kept damage minimal (o4 qualifies w12). Packet/caption anomaly: F6 caption assigns (c) lower and (d) upper, but panel labels read c = 15 U (OP 27.44%) and d = 15 L (21.65%); text follows the labels. Cement dissolution (w9) typed STR/microstructure/damage (poor; aspect=binder dissolution): environmental loss of grain-to-grain continuity whose next step is sanding off, not a phase-amount argument; see broadening proposal. Lost: capillary absorption/drying kinetics, mass-gain tables, efflorescence timing and heights, K-sulfate details."
}